Text: [13] published the largest dataset for human activity recognition. They proposed an extension of long short term memory (LSTM) model which leverages group motion of several body joints to recognize human activity from skeletal data. A different adaptation of the LSTM model was proposed by Liu et al. [14] where spatial interaction among joints was considered in addition to the temporal dynamics. Veeriah et al. [15] proposed a LSTM network to capture the salient motion pattern of body joints.

