Text: In summary, the contributions of this work are: • We propose an RNN architecture with a novel spatial data augmentation technique. • We propose an architecture which uses both RGB and skeletal data to improve recognition accuracy. • We introduce and publicly release a multi–modal dataset for ASL called GMU-ASL51. II. LITERATURE REVIEW Most sign language recognition systems use RGB video data as input. These approaches model sequential dependencies using Hidden Markov Models (HMM).

